WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.867
So there is no doubt

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.002
the decision to indict

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:02.635
has elicited

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:03.937
a strong reaction

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.972
across the political spectrum.

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.874
New CNN polling shows many Americans

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.009
believe politics played

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.977
at least some role in the decision

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.212
to indict Donald Trump.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:12.846
Take a look at this.

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:16.116
52% say politics played a major role.

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:18.451
And you see. 23% say a minor role.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.486
Some think no role

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:21.087
and there's also an element of people

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:23.156
still they really are not sure.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.391
CNN's Jeff Zeleny joins

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:26.092
us now for much more on this.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.394
Jeff, many people think people

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:28.261
that politics

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:31.431
played some role in this indictment,

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.666
but how many people,

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:34.200
how many people

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:34.801
that were polled

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:38.238
actually approve of the indictment?

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:39.072
This is so interesting.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.774
Of course, you cannot divorce politics

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:41.608
from any of this

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:42.976
because we were talking about

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:43.910
the former president

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:44.277
here, who,

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.979
of course, is a current candidate

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:46.546
for the White House.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.781
But when you look at the findings

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:50.083
of our new poll, take a look at this.

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.985
60% of Americans,

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:54.220
some six in ten of Americans support

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.423
the overall indictment here.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:58.124
And 40% are against it.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.527
That's largely driven by

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:00.827
sort of

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.162
some common views from Republicans.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:02.996
Of course, they're opposed

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:03.963
Democrats support,

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.331
but independents largely

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.200
follow this rule.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.435
So that is so interesting.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:08.601
That.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:09.903
60% support

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:10.937
and we should be clear,

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.205
we do not know exactly

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.339
what is in the indictment.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:14.908
This is just based on the broad

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.010
confines of a familiar storyline

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:18.244
of a hush money payment

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.746
that we've been talking about

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:21.347
for more than six years now.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.583
So six in ten Americans support that.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:24.584
But there is so much

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:25.852
more interesting findings

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:27.387
in our poll

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:27.821
this morning that

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:28.354
really speaks

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.223
to the dynamic of the politics

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.257
going into this, Kate.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:33.126
And one thing we see is the one thing

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:33.726
maybe the

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:36.062
the only unsurprising thing in

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:36.663
this is that

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.898
it shows that the nation is remains

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:39.766
so divided,

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.401
especially when it comes to Donald Trump.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:42.135
But what

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:42.602
what is it

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:43.937
what are you seeing in this poll

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.538
in terms of the overall impact,

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:46.439
the impact on the country,

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:49.075
the impact on democracy?

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:50.810
We should talk about the historic

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.479
nature of this. Yes.

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:52.745
You know,

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:53.880
this is a

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.348
really run of the mill indictment,

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:57.550
but a former president has never been

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.852
indicted and arraigned.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.053
So the next 48 hours

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.821
are going to see something in the country

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.556
we have never seen before.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.191
So when you talk about democracy,

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.426
take a look at these numbers.

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:08.361
What do you think about the strength

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:09.796
of democracy?

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.798
And 31% of Americans

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:13.133
say that it strengthens.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.667
31% say it weakens.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.703
23%, it has no effect at all.

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.238
So divided Americans

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:20.974
clearly divided among party lines

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:22.876
and familiar lines on this.

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:24.811
But this is a historic proceeding.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:25.545
No question.

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:26.546
So we cannot

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.081
not take stock of all of that.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.483
But there is no doubt as we go forward

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.685
here, democracy is at the core of this.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:33.987
And the

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.023
he obviously has other

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.625
cases pending in Georgia

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.059
and in federal court as well.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:40.760
So this is something

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.028
that will be a through line

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:43.930
of all this conversation today, Kate.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.632
That's that is and that is a great point.

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:46.366
It's good to see you, Jeff.

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:47.700
Thank you so much.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.536
CNN's Chris Cornell is outside

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:51.704
the court in New York City for us.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.306
Corrupt officials in New York

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.041
are set to make a public announcement

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.210
that we're just hearing the commissioner

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.178
and the mayor.

00:02:58.178 --> 00:02:59.913
What are you learning

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.183
Yes, Sara, that's right.

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.851
So it just fell at noon Eastern.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:05.685
New York City mayor

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.286
and the

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:07.453
NYPD commissioner

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:08.054
are expected

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:08.988
to make an announcement

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:09.856
to address the public

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:11.457
about the security measures

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:12.392
that are in place

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:14.460
for Trump's arraignment tomorrow.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.862
Now, sources tell bringing

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.730
Grasp that there are no credible threats

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.465
against the courthouse or in the area

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.534
and there's no threat of disrupting

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.635
But they will give the public

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.170
a briefing of what to expect

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.405
now behind the scenes.

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:27.407
There's a lot that's also happening.

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:28.274
There's restrictions

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.876
on the 15th floor in the courthouse

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.311
behind me over my shoulder.

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.812
That is where the former president

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:33.980
will be arraigned,

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:37.383
come in, self surrender midday.

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:39.152
And they were speeding up this process.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:41.321
He may or may not have a mug shot taken.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:42.789
There are questions about that.

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:44.057
He's likely to be fingerprinted

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:44.791
and then he will

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.259
walk down a public hallway

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.260
where other defendants,

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.728
everyone from drug dealers

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.830
to his former chief financial officer

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.165
and go into the courtroom

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:53.032
and face the judge,

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.067
that's when the judge

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.301
will ask him to enter a plea.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:56.002
And Trump's attorneys

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:57.837
say that he will plead not guilty.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:58.371
From there,

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.105
Trump is expected

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:00.673
to head back to the airport

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:01.641
and then back to Mar

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:02.809
a Lago, where he said

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:05.044
he will address the nation at eight 15.

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:05.878
Sara

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.815
arraignments a regular course of business

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:10.917
for the courts, but not this one.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:12.418
Can you give us a sense of what Trump's

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.586
legal team has been saying?

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.021
They have done a media blitz over

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:15.888
the last few days.

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:19.892
Yeah, they certainly have.

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.160
And I mean, their main point here

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.462
is that they are going to look

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:23.796
for every possible way

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:26.165
to launch a legal challenge in this case

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:27.300
put going ahead

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.334
that they're putting forward

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.769
an aggressive posture.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:30.737
Now, one thing

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:32.405
that one of Trump's attorneys,

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:33.573
Joe Tacopina,

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.241
he was on CNN yesterday

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.343
and saying, you know, just how aggressive

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:38.311
they're going to take this.

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:39.579
Take a listen.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:42.915
We will take the indictment.

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.417
We will dissect it.

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:47.720
The team will look at every every

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.521
potential issue

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.523
that we will be able to challenge

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:51.090
and we will challenge.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:51.557
And, of course,

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:53.059
I very much anticipate

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.127
a motion to dismiss coming

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:57.330
because there's no law that fits this

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.097
at all.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.567
So they're looking to take a bunch of

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:02.568
legal angles here.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:03.636
Motions to dismiss,

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:04.837
also possibly challenging

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:06.939
the statute of limitations in this case.

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.074
So what other matters?

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:09.108
Now, the one thing, though, is

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:09.842
that those motions

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.344
will all happen a bit down the road

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:12.645
because we've yet to see

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.080
what the specific charges

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.448
are in this indictment.

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:16.015
And CNN

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.250
and other media organizations

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.118
have asked the judge to unseal that.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.353
The judge just has a deadline

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:22.188
for both sides that Trump and the D.A.

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:23.523
to respond at 1 p.m..

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:25.425
And we could see these specific charges

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:27.293
and the indictment unsealed later today.

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:29.562
Sara, Kara Scannell, thank you.

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:31.831
Outside of the court there in New York.

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:32.799
I want to bring in CNN

00:05:32.799 --> 00:05:34.934
national correspondent Kristen Holmes.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.536
You are in West Palm Beach, Florida,

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:37.970
as we can see

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.473
with the wind and the water behind you.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.642
The president is set to take off

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.410
in, I think, less than an hour.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.745
What are you learning about his plan?

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:49.082
Sara?

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:49.882
That's absolutely right.

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.084
So we are waiting to see him

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.652
leave his Mar a Lago home.

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:53.486
He will be traveling

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:55.621
