00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:08.167
And they are expected

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:10.136
to land around 3:00.

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:10.937
Then we are told

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:12.372
Trump will go to Trump Tower.

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:14.440
And I was actually just told by a source

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:15.174
that he is likely

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:16.376
to meet with his lawyers

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:17.910
while he is in Trump Tower.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.812
He will spend the night there before

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:22.048
heading to the courthouse on Tuesday.

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:24.817
Now, as you noted and as Kara noted,

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:27.353
he will come back almost immediately

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:28.821
after that arraignment

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:30.423
to deliver remarks.

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:31.657
He will be there at Mar

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:32.792
a Lago at his resort.

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:34.026
And I am told by sources

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.094
this will be the former

00:06:35.094 --> 00:06:36.562
president's opportunity

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:38.564
to really take control of the narrative.

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:39.165
Of course,

00:06:39.165 --> 00:06:39.966
we have heard him

00:06:39.966 --> 00:06:41.067
from the last several weeks

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:42.568
calling this a political witch

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:43.870
hunt a hoax.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:45.338
But this will be the first time

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:46.606
that we actually see him

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:48.708
respond to the charges

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:50.176
as we all learn them on

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:50.977
Tuesday afternoon.

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:52.145
That's what we're expected to

00:06:52.145 --> 00:06:53.513
actually learn what they are.

00:06:55.148 --> 00:06:55.481
All right.

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:56.349
Christine Holmes, thank you

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:58.351
there live from West Palm Beach.

00:06:58.351 --> 00:06:59.252
Let's go ahead and dig deeper

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:00.987
into the security concerns now.

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:02.955
Joining us is Jonathan Wackrow.

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:04.290
He is CNN law enforcement

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:05.224
analyst and

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:06.926
a former Secret Service agent.

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:08.494
So you know this

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:09.362
like the back of your hand,

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:11.531
except this is unprecedented.

00:07:11.531 --> 00:07:12.031
Let's talk

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:13.232
about what's going to happen here.

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:15.268
Usually the Secret Service is in charge

00:07:15.535 --> 00:07:16.436
of presidents, former

00:07:16.436 --> 00:07:17.637
presidents, vice presidents,

00:07:17.637 --> 00:07:18.771
and they're the ones that sort of make

00:07:18.771 --> 00:07:19.739
the plan.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.274
Is that going to be different now?

00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:22.208
It is different now.

00:07:22.208 --> 00:07:24.310
The Secret Service is not the lead

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:26.913
coordinating agency for this.

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:28.314
The security protocols

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:29.782
that we see being put into place, it's

00:07:29.782 --> 00:07:31.584
actually the NYPD

00:07:31.584 --> 00:07:33.019
is taking the lead role

00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:34.153
along with the New York

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:35.488
state court officers

00:07:35.488 --> 00:07:36.956
They're really bifurcating

00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:38.758
the internal security of the courthouse

00:07:38.758 --> 00:07:41.127
and then external in the city at large.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:42.995
And that's unique for the Secret Service.

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:44.630
Typically, we do see them in that lead,

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:45.698
coordinating role,

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:47.166
whether it's for political

00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:49.001
rallies, presidential events.

00:07:49.001 --> 00:07:50.036
But this is different.

00:07:50.036 --> 00:07:51.204
This is a private event.

00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:52.605
This is private business

00:07:52.605 --> 00:07:53.539
that the former president

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:55.408
has to do in front of the court.

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:57.243
So from the Secret Service standpoint,

00:07:57.243 --> 00:07:58.611
it's almost administrative.

00:07:58.611 --> 00:07:59.545
Their responsibility

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:00.680
is the protectee

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:02.081
bringing him from point A

00:08:02.081 --> 00:08:03.349
into the courthouse,

00:08:03.349 --> 00:08:04.450
allowing the former president

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:06.385
to do his business before the court

00:08:06.385 --> 00:08:08.154
and getting out all safely,

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:09.789
but very well coordinated

00:08:09.789 --> 00:08:12.325
with other law enforcement entities

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:12.692
who are

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:13.593
who are participating

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:14.527
in tomorrow's event.

00:08:14.527 --> 00:08:15.628
I am curious

00:08:15.628 --> 00:08:16.762
how long it has taken

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:17.830
for them to coordinate,

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.432
knowing all of this

00:08:19.432 --> 00:08:20.333
that has been happening

00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:21.667
in the lead up to this.

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:22.902
But I do want to ask you

00:08:22.902 --> 00:08:24.370
what their concerns are.

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:26.305
I mean, there are a myriad of things

00:08:26.305 --> 00:08:27.306
that could happen

00:08:27.306 --> 00:08:29.742
when you have a city the size of New York

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:32.144
with the speed at which New York,

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:33.312
you know, flows.

00:08:33.312 --> 00:08:35.181
What are the big security concerns

00:08:35.181 --> 00:08:36.616
that they should be looking out for?

00:08:36.616 --> 00:08:37.817
Really, you have to think about.

00:08:37.817 --> 00:08:39.652
We've known about tomorrow for a while.

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:41.220
Right. We anticipated it.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:42.154
So law enforcement

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:43.556
has been coordinating,

00:08:43.556 --> 00:08:45.992
putting together security plan

00:08:45.992 --> 00:08:47.126
the overlay of the city.

00:08:47.126 --> 00:08:49.095
So not just at the courthouse,

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:50.563
but the city at large.

00:08:50.563 --> 00:08:51.797
The challenge is addressing

00:08:51.797 --> 00:08:52.932
the wild card events.

00:08:52.932 --> 00:08:53.733
What happens

00:08:53.733 --> 00:08:55.568
if there's peaceful protests

00:08:55.568 --> 00:08:57.637
that actually turns into,

00:08:57.637 --> 00:08:58.471
you know, violence?

00:08:58.471 --> 00:08:59.272
What happens?

00:08:59.272 --> 00:09:00.673
It's consequence management.

00:09:00.673 --> 00:09:01.774
But the NYPD

00:09:01.774 --> 00:09:03.209
does this better than any other law

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:05.011
enforcement entity in the world.

00:09:05.011 --> 00:09:06.045
They're prepared.

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:06.879
Tomorrow you'll see

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:09.849
35,000 uniformed NYPD officers

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:11.851
in a 24 hour period,

00:09:11.851 --> 00:09:13.419
making sure that the city is safe.

00:09:13.419 --> 00:09:14.220
And secure.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:14.887
They're going to play it

00:09:14.887 --> 00:09:16.856
extremely cautious. Why?

00:09:16.856 --> 00:09:17.924
Because law enforcement

00:09:17.924 --> 00:09:19.825
no longer has to anticipate

00:09:19.825 --> 00:09:20.960
whether or not

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:21.861
domestic violence

00:09:21.861 --> 00:09:23.663
extremists will actually engage

00:09:23.663 --> 00:09:25.665
We know from January six that they will.

00:09:25.932 --> 00:09:28.334
So they have to overprepare tomorrow,

00:09:28.534 --> 00:09:30.369
prepare for the worst case scenario.

00:09:30.369 --> 00:09:31.203
Hope for the best.

00:09:31.203 --> 00:09:33.272
Hopefully it's peaceful protests

00:09:33.272 --> 00:09:33.873
individuals

00:09:33.873 --> 00:09:35.274
expressing their First Amendment

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:36.542
constitutional right.

00:09:36.542 --> 00:09:38.644
But it doesn't transcend into violence.

00:09:38.844 --> 00:09:41.047
And we know very similar to January six,

00:09:41.047 --> 00:09:41.781
you were hearing

00:09:41.781 --> 00:09:42.615
from the former president,

00:09:42.615 --> 00:09:43.149
he is

00:09:43.149 --> 00:09:44.450
calling on people to

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:46.686
to be there to support him.

00:09:46.686 --> 00:09:49.021
I do want to ask you about this sort of,

00:09:49.188 --> 00:09:51.357
you know, mandate that every agency has

00:09:52.024 --> 00:09:54.093
and everything is political

00:09:54.093 --> 00:09:55.094
at some point, right,

00:09:55.094 --> 00:09:56.295
when you're dealing with

00:09:56.295 --> 00:09:57.930
a former president.

00:09:57.930 --> 00:09:59.065
And certainly he's made it

00:09:59.065 --> 00:10:01.133
so posting on social media.

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:02.802
So when it comes to Donald Trump

00:10:02.802 --> 00:10:04.370
and when it comes to the Secret Service

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.739
handling this particular unprecedented

00:10:06.739 --> 00:10:08.174
historic case,

00:10:08.174 --> 00:10:08.941
how do they do it

00:10:08.941 --> 00:10:10.509
without getting sucked into the politics?

00:10:10.509 --> 00:10:10.876
Well, listen,

00:10:10.876 --> 00:10:12.378
there's no other law enforcement entity

00:10:12.378 --> 00:10:14.313
in the world that's drawn into politics

00:10:14.313 --> 00:10:15.881
more than the Secret Service. Right.

00:10:15.881 --> 00:10:16.949
By the nature of their job,

00:10:16.949 --> 00:10:17.984
they're at the White House.

00:10:17.984 --> 00:10:20.119
They're with political leaders.

00:10:20.119 --> 00:10:21.554
But this is a seminal moment

00:10:21.554 --> 00:10:22.288
for the agency

00:10:22.288 --> 00:10:24.290
where they have to remain neutral.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:25.591
The optic has to show

00:10:25.591 --> 00:10:26.525
that they're not currying

00:10:26.525 --> 00:10:27.860
favor to the former president

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:28.828
nor the D.A.

00:10:28.828 --> 00:10:29.695
They need to focus

00:10:29.695 --> 00:10:31.097
on their primary remit,

00:10:31.097 --> 00:10:32.231
which is protection

00:10:32.231 --> 00:10:34.033
protecting the former president,

00:10:34.033 --> 00:10:34.634
because that's

00:10:34.634 --> 00:10:36.102
what they're mandated to do.

00:10:36.102 --> 00:10:37.603
They work with other law enforcement

00:10:37.603 --> 00:10:38.504
entities to ensure

00:10:38.504 --> 00:10:40.306
that the area is secure,

00:10:40.306 --> 00:10:42.008
but they are not coordinating

00:10:42.008 --> 00:10:43.342
any special accommodations

00:10:43.342 --> 00:10:44.510
for the president inside.

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:45.945
The moment that they do.

00:10:45.945 --> 00:10:46.912
They'll they'll be swayed

00:10:46.912 --> 00:10:47.713
one way or the other.

00:10:47.713 --> 00:10:48.481
And right now,

00:10:48.481 --> 00:10:49.715
it is essential

00:10:49.715 --> 00:10:50.683
for the agency

00:10:50.683 --> 00:10:52.151
just to do their core

00:10:52.151 --> 00:10:53.552
responsibility of protection.

